          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        setup: {
          players: '6 or 8 players divided into two teams of equal size. Teams sit alternately, each player between two opponents.',
          deck: "Remove the four 8s from a standard 52-card deck, leaving 48 cards. These form eight 'half-suits' (also called sets or books).",
          equipment: 'Standard deck. No writing materials allowed.',
          dealing: 'Shuffle thoroughly and deal all cards one at a time face down. For 6 players: 8 cards each. For 8 players: 6 cards each.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Collect and claim more half-suits than the opposing team. Each claimed half-suit scores 1 point.',
          gameplay: "1. **Asking**: On your turn, ask any one specific player from the OTHER team for a specific card. A question is valid ONLY if: (a) You ask for a specific card (by value and suit), (b) You have another card in that half-suit in your hand, (c) The player you ask holds at least one card, (d) You do NOT ask for a card that is in your own hand. 2. **Successful Ask**: If the asked player has the card, they pass it to you face-up, and you keep the turn, asking another question. 3. **Failed Ask**: If the asked player does NOT have the card, your turn ends and it becomes their turn to ask. 4. **No Teammate Asking**: You may NEVER ask a teammate for a card. All questions must be directed to the opposing team. 5. **Claiming**: If you believe your team holds all 6 cards of a half-suit, you may claim it on your turn by saying 'Claim' and naming exactly who has which cards. If correct, your team scores the half-suit. If you state the location of even one card wrongly, the half-suit is cancelled and neither team gets it.",
          keyRules: [
            '48 cards total (no 8s). 8 half-suits: Low/High of each suit (2-7 and 9-A).',
            'Must have another card from the half-suit to ask for a card.',
            'Cannot ask teammates; only opponents.',
            'Successful ask = continue turn; failed ask = turn passes.',
            'Claim by naming exactly who has which cards in a half-suit.',
            'Failed claim = half-suit cancelled (neither team gets it).',
            'No note-taking allowedâ€”pure memory only.',
            'Game ends when all 8 half-suits claimed or no cards remain.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Listen to every question. If Player A asks Player B for the 5 of Spades, you now know that Player A has at least one Low Spade (2-7) and Player B does NOT have the 5 of Spades. Memorize this information.',
          intermediate: "The False Scent: If you have four cards of a half-suit, and you know an opponent is tracking you, ask for a card in a DIFFERENT half-suit where you only have one card. This confuses their tracking of your 'power' suits. Negative Inference: If Player A asks Player B for a card and B doesn't have it, and later Player C asks Player D for the same card and D doesn't have it, you know the card must be with one of the remaining opponents.",
          advanced: "Declarer's Coordination: Don't declare too early. If you know your partner has the 9 of Hearts but you aren't sure about the 10, ask for the 10. Even if you miss, your partner now knows YOU have Hearts and can follow up. The 'Loaded Question': If you have 5 of the 6 cards in a half-suit, ask for the 6th card from an opponent who you suspect has it. If they give it to you, claim immediately. If not, you've learned who doesn't have it, narrowing down the location.",
          tips: [
            "Mentally 'label' cards. Spades 2-7 = 'Low Spades'. Spades 9-A = 'High Spades'. Never mix them up.",
            'Track the count of cards each player has. Sudden drops indicate successful claims or many cards given away.',
            'If an opponent asks for a card you have, note which teammate they were askingâ€”they may be coordinating.',
            "Don't claim unless you're at least 90% sure. A failed claim gives the opponents a free half-suit.",
            "The 8s are removedâ€”don't waste mental energy looking for them!",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
