          deckDescription: 'A standard 52-card French deck with the four 8s removed, leaving 48 cards. Four suits (Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, Spades); each suit is split into two half-suits: low (2-3-4-5-6-7) and high (9-10-J-Q-K-A). Used for Literature and similar quartet games.',
          suitDescription: 'French suits: Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, Spades. Each suit has twelve ranks in play (no 8s), forming eight half-suits of six cards each.',
          rankDescription: 'Stripped 48: ranks 2 through 7 (low half-suit) and 9, 10, J, Q, K, A (high half-suit) per suit; 8s are removed from the deck.',
