        prompts: {
          human: "Welcome to Literatureâ€”the ultimate test of memory and deduction! You're on a team, and your goal is to collect all six cards of a 'half-suit' (like Low Spades: 2-3-4-5-6-7). Ask opponents for specific cards, but you must hold another card from that half-suit to ask. Remember every question and answerâ€”no notes allowed! When you think your team has all six cards of a half-suit, declare itâ€”but be wrong, and the opponents get it!",
          ai: 'Game: Literature. 6 or 8 players, 2 teams. 48-card deck (no 8s). 8 half-suits (Low/High of each suit: 2-7 and 9-A). Deal 8 cards each (6 players) or 6 each (8 players). Ask opponents for specific cards; must hold another from that half-suit. Successful ask = continue; failed = turn passes. Can claim half-suit by naming exactly who has which cards. Wrong claim = opponents get it. No note-taking. Most half-suits wins.',
